Q: How do I create a dictionary of dictionaries in Python? A: <p>You don't need to read the entire file into memory (<code>f.readlines()</code>)</p>
<p>You can parameterise the flow like this:</p>
<pre><code>FILENAME = &quot;data.txt&quot;
KEYS = [&quot;Name&quot;, &quot;Line1&quot;, &quot;Line2&quot;]

output = {}

with open(FILENAME) as f:
    for lineno, linetext in enumerate(f):
        if (i := lineno % len(KEYS)) == 0:
            k = lineno // len(KEYS) + 1
            output.update({k: {}})
        output[k][KEYS[i]] = linetext.strip()
</code></pre>

Q: css geometry math: clip path margin polygon triangles- why the right margin or right-1 does not work, if left-1 is used A: <p>You can find the triangle you are looking for within my collection: <a href="https://css-generators.com/triangle-shapes/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://css-generators.com/triangle-shapes/</a>. I already did the calculation</p>
<p>It's #21</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>.triangle {
  --b:15px;  /* control the border thickness */

  width: 250px;
  aspect-ratio: 1;
  clip-path: polygon(0 0,100% 0,0 100%,0 0,var(--b) var(--b),var(--b) calc(100% - var(--b)/tan(22.5deg)),calc(100% - var(--b)/tan(22.5deg)) var(--b),var(--b) var(--b));
  background: linear-gradient(45deg,#FA6900,#C02942);
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div class="triangle"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
<p>And if you want to fill it. Move the code to a pseudo element and use #17 on the main element</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>.triangle {
  --b:15px;  /* control the border thickness */

  width: 250px;
  aspect-ratio: 1;
  display: inline-grid;
  background: blue;
  clip-path: polygon(0 0,100% 0,0 100%);
}
.triangle:before {
  content:"";
  clip-path: polygon(0 0,100% 0,0 100%,0 0,var(--b) var(--b),var(--b) calc(100% - var(--b)/tan(22.5deg)),calc(100% - var(--b)/tan(22.5deg)) var(--b),var(--b) var(--b));
  background: red;
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div class="triangle"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
<p>And if you only want the left and right part:</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>.triangle {
  --b:15px;  /* control the border thickness */

  width: 250px;
  aspect-ratio: 1;
  display: inline-grid;
  background: blue;
  clip-path: polygon(0 0,100% 0,0 100%);
}
.triangle:before {
  content:"";
  clip-path: polygon(0 0,100% 0,0 100%,0 0,var(--b) 0,var(--b) calc(100% - var(--b)/tan(22.5deg)),calc(100% - var(--b)/cos(45deg)) 0,var(--b) 0);
  background: red;
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div class="triangle"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>

Q: Next.js Middleware updates cookie but React Server Component still reads old value until full reload A: <p>You must use async function and first you must get cookie function:</p>
<pre><code>export default async function Page() {
    const cookieStore = await cookies();
    const org = cookieStore().get(&quot;active-org&quot;)?.value
}
</code></pre>
